# Game detail art wash (locked)

The signed-in game description view uses a **full-main blurred cover wash**. This look is approved for **both light and dark**. Do not revert it or restyle it toward milky light-mode ink.

## Backdrop

- Cover fills the full `.library` shell (`.library-wash`) — behind the sidebar pill **and** main (search, profile, nav), not only the description block.
- Sharp cover stays in the media slot.
- Dark: black-tinted overlay so color still shows.
- Light: **no white/gray milk**. Tiny darken only (`rgba(18, 20, 26, 0.06)`). Keep saturation so the art color reads like dark mode.

## Chrome on the wash (both themes)

Cover art is dark. Type stays **light-on-dark** (white / near-white). Frost glass differs by theme via `--wash-frost*` on `.library--game`:

- **Light:** white frost (`rgba(255,255,255,~0.16)`).
- **Dark:** deeper bluish frost (`rgba(24,34,52,~0.58)` + cool blue border) — not the same white glass as light.
- Tags, Back, favorite gem (off), search, profile, menu, profile dropdown, **sidebar pill** (desktop + narrow): use those frost tokens + white type. Not solid opaque slabs.
- Favorite gem on: red gem / red glass glow — never dark ink.
- Play: **white button, dark label** (`#ffffff` / `#12141a`).

## Do not

- Dark title/description/Play on the wash in light mode (vanishes on dark covers).
- Heavy white overlays that bleach the blur.
- Solid white search/profile slabs on the wash.

Implementation: `.library-main--game` in `LibraryView.css`. Back from GameDetail fades the wash and chrome (~420ms); do not snap to the library palette.
